{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**, Rule 6c‑11 requires a **free, publicly accessible website** disclosing:\n\n- **Holdings before regular trading opens** on the primary listing exchange each business day: the portfolio underlying that day’s NAV calculations, including ticker, CUSIP/other identifier, description, quantity and portfolio weight.\n- **Prior-business-day NAV/share, market price, and premium/discount.**\n- **Premium/discount history:** a table counting premium and discount days, plus a daily premium/discount line graph, covering the most recently completed calendar year and completed calendar quarters since that year.\n- **Median bid–ask spread for the latest 30 calendar days.**\n- **Sustained deviations:** if premium or discount exceeds 2% for **more than seven consecutive trading days**, a statement identifying that occurrence and discussion of factors reasonably believed materially responsible; retain both online for at least one year thereafter.\n\n**Holdings are not transaction baskets:** creation/redemption baskets may differ; Rule 6c‑11 does not require their public website disclosure."}}
